# Portable artifact routing bundle

This directory is the project-owned source of truth for artifact location and
format. It remains readable after any setup tool or plugin has been removed.

## Read in this order

1. `artifact-routing.json` identifies the project mode, applications, ownership
   roots and the two host-local adapter states.
2. `artifact-format-contract.json` defines the required metadata and path rules
   for a generated artifact.
3. The application routing instruction at `{{ROUTING_INSTRUCTION}}` is the
   detailed, app-scoped routing authority.

## Host-local adapters

The shared bundle is under `.ai-docs/harness/`; host-local files are intentionally
separate:

- Claude: `.claude/settings.json` and `.claude/hooks/claude-pre-tool-use.ps1`
- Codex: `.codex/hooks.json` and `.codex/hooks/codex-pre-tool-use.ps1`

Both remain `pending-trust` until an administrator approves host installation
and the host-specific trust step. `install-routing.ps1 -Plan` is safe to run:
it emits the identical proposed local targets and does not write files.

The manifest `pending-trust`/`active` state records trust evidence only. Codex
decides execution from its own `/hooks` trusted hash (or a per-invocation
`--dangerously-bypass-hook-trust`), so a `pending-trust` hook may already run.
Re-running `-Apply` keeps `active` only while the host config hash is unchanged.

The Codex hook matches only `apply_patch|Bash`. It prints nothing on allow, a
`systemMessage` on bypass, and a `hookEventName=PreToolUse` deny response (exit 0)
on deny or when the adapter or core fails.

## Write guard boundary

The adapters share a project-owned path guard. It permits existing canonical
documents, approved app source, `.ai-docs/_inbox/**`, and declared exceptions. A
new managed document requires a path-bound, content-hash-bound, one-shot marker
created with `approve-artifact.ps1 -Approve`; it expires and is consumed after
one exact write. Dynamic shell targets are recorded as bypass evidence, not
claimed as fully enforced. Hosted tools, opt-out tool paths, shell redirects
created after command execution, and processes outside this project are also
best-effort limits rather than a complete security boundary.

## External artifact normalization

`normalize-artifact.ps1 -Plan` previews a G12 proposal. With explicit
`-Promote -ApprovePromotion`, text formats (`.md`, `.mdx`, `.txt`, `.rst`,
`.adoc`, `.asciidoc`) are UTF-8 normalized and use a marker-aware merge that
preserves existing unmanaged text. JSON/YAML, images, and PDF stay in
`.ai-docs/_inbox/{artifact-bundle-id}/artifact-manifest.json`; the tool refuses a
lossy automatic conversion or canonical promotion for those fixed formats.

## Recovery and review

Do not copy an adapter or configuration from one host to the other. Inspect the
host-specific input contract in its adapter, review the plan, then apply the
approved host-specific merge workflow. A proposal from `.ai-docs/_inbox/` remains
non-canonical until its provenance and target path are explicitly approved.
